# Snap_12 rows [6, 8, 206, 16, 288, 265, 294]: Type, written Mvir (float) and SimulationHaloIndex
# (SAGE26 writes llabs of the halo's MostBoundID, src/io/save_gals_hdf5.c:878; none is negative)
# as MostBoundID, written Regime; Zcurr ZZ[12], snapnum 12. Each row enters the call with
# mergeType 0 (rows merge in the substeps, after the classification) and its input FFBRegime
# seeded to the opposite of the written value, so the write is visible. call.has_reference 1: the
# oracle refuses the fixture unless SAGE26's FFBRegime equals the written value of every row.
# Reachability: R6-reachable (real rows; the input FFBRegime seeded)
format sage26-oracle-fixture 1
